      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Frank Kovalchek from Anchorage, Alaska, USA",
      "description": "I took these photos in August 2009 during a hike to Lost Lake. This is an excellent but long trail outside of Seward, Alaska. We did a traverse, starting on the north side and exiting from the south side. It was still about 15 miles long with a bit of a climb on the way in. The day started off rainy and gray but got a lot better as we kept climbing. One of the major benefits was all the ripe blueberries on the trail - and they were so sweet - just like me!",
